module

public import Rule30Open.Columns.LockBlocks

/-!
# Steering sequences force locks for 23 blocks of period 12

[LockBlocks](LockBlocks.md) turns a check the kernel evaluates, `lockCheckB`, into a lock of the finite game: once the
center column repeats a block, column 14 never reads a steering sequence. Here the check runs on the 23 blocks of
period 12 that neither the game at width 14 nor the kit excludes and whose game at width 13 has locked windows
that every window can be steered into, from `computations/locks.py`.

* `steered12`: the entries `Steered`, each block as its least rotation with its sequence and the windows where the
  sequence leaves each start; `steered12_check`: every check passes.
* `center_lock_steered12`: once the center column repeats one of the blocks from time `T`, read from any phase,
  column 14 does not read the block's sequence from any time `t₀ ≥ T`.
* `not_eventually_steered12`: so if column 14 reads the sequence at arbitrarily late times, the center column does
  not eventually repeat the block, in the kit's form `EventuallyWord`.

The natural-language argument is `LockBlocks12.md`, beside this file.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Rule30Open

open Ruliology.CellularAutomata LockWord LockBlocks

namespace LockBlocks

set_option Elab.async false

